USC: don't turn an UNPCKVEC with a source modifier into a MOV

VMOVReplaceArguments replaced an UNPCKVEC of scalar sources by a MOV even
when the UNPCKVEC negated or took the absolute value of its source, which a
MOV can't do, so fabs() and the like were lost (fmod and pow of negative
values).  Keep the UNPCKVEC; FixVectorSourceModifiers lowers the modifier.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c b/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c
index 0da4a83..8b3f0ee 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c
@@ -8107,7 +8107,12 @@ static IMG_BOOL VMOVReplaceArguments(PINTERMEDIATE_STATE	psState,
 
 	if (!bCheckOnly)
 	{
-		if (psInst->eOpcode == IUNPCKVEC && psContext->bScalarSources)
+		/*
+			A MOV can't apply the unpack's source modifier: keep the UNPCKVEC
+			(FixVectorSourceModifiers lowers it later).
+		*/
+		if (psInst->eOpcode == IUNPCKVEC && psContext->bScalarSources &&
+			!psInst->u.psVec->asSrcMod[0].bNegate && !psInst->u.psVec->asSrcMod[0].bAbs)
 		{
 			if (psInst->u.psVec->aeSrcFmt[0] == UF_REGFORMAT_F32)
 			{
